IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qlt-core`

-- Land Tax Act 2010 (Queensland), with the Land Tax Regulation 2021 and the Taxation Administration Act 2001 -- the
-- questions of the INDIVIDUAL WHO OWNS LAND: a home owner, the owner of other land, or an absentee owner.
--
-- SEAT: the individual land owner. "Do I owe land tax this year? Is my home exempt, and what if I rent out a room or
-- work from home? What if I am moving house, renovating or in care? How much do I owe on my investment land, and more
-- as an absentee? When must I tell the Commissioner? Can I pay by instalments? How do I object?" Every question is
-- phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in qlt-core.l4; this module
-- builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no rule: every test, deadline and date it gives is a core
-- function (the last days are counted by the same clocks as the core's regulative rules). Where the law leaves a
-- judgment to the Commissioner, the answer says so ("..., if the Commissioner is satisfied ...") rather than guessing it.
--
-- Groups (§§) follow the Acts' order. A group whose comment says SITUATION only arises for some owners (moving house,
-- renovating, farming, a deceased estate, working abroad, an objection); the form can ask "Has this happened to you?"
-- before showing it.
--
-- Conventions: a financial year is named by the year it starts (2026 for 2026-27); dates are calendar dates; money is
-- in Australian dollars.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land tax -- the individual land owner's questions`

DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no: this section does not require me to give notice`

§§ `Do I owe land tax this financial year? (ss 6 to 9, 16 to 19, 22, 31, 32, Schedules 1 and 3)`

@export When does my land tax liability for a financial year arise (s 7)?
GIVEN `the year the financial year starts` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year starts on 1 July (2026 for the 2026-27 financial year)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does my land tax liability arise` IS
    `the liability date for the financial year starting in` `the year the financial year starts`

@export Am I the owner of this land for land tax, at midnight on 30 June (ss 8, 10, 11, 13, 14)?
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Position in relation to the land` @desc Your position at midnight on 30 June: one of "entitled to a freehold estate in the land, alone or with others, and in possession"; "entitled to receive rents and profits from the land"; "the seller under an agreement for sale, the buyer not yet in possession"; "the seller under an agreement for sale, the buyer in possession"; "the buyer under an agreement for sale, in possession"; "the buyer under an agreement for sale, not yet in possession"; "entitled to a life estate in possession"; "entitled to the fee simple in reversion or remainder after a life estate"; "a mortgagee, whether or not in possession"; "none of these"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I the owner of this land for land tax` IF
    `the person is the owner (ss 10, 11, 13, 14)` `my position`

@export Is this land taxable land (s 9)?
GIVEN `the land is in Queensland`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is in Queensland
      `the land is freehold`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land has been granted by the State as freehold (an estate in fee simple), rather than being State leasehold or reserve
      `the land is exempt land`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is exempt, for example as your home or as primary production land (see those questions)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this land taxable land` IF
    `it is taxable land (s 9)` `the land is in Queensland` `the land is freehold` `the land is exempt land`

@export What is the taxable value of this land for the financial year (ss 16 to 18)?
GIVEN `this year's valuation`                              IS A NUMBER  @desc The land's value under the Land Valuation Act 2010 at midnight on 30 June starting the financial year, in dollars (the Valuer-General's valuation)
      `there are valuations for the 2 previous years`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land also had a Land Valuation Act value for each of the 2 previous financial years
      `last year's valuation`                              IS A NUMBER  @desc The land's Land Valuation Act value for the previous financial year, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the valuation for the year before last`             IS A NUMBER  @desc The land's Land Valuation Act value for the financial year before that, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the averaging factor for the year`                  IS A NUMBER  @desc The s 18(2) averaging factor for the financial year, used only where the 2 earlier valuations are missing (a statewide number to 2 decimal places, e.g. 0.92)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the taxable value of this land` IS
    `the taxable value (s 16)` `this year's valuation` `there are valuations for the 2 previous years` `last year's valuation` `the valuation for the year before last` `the averaging factor for the year`

@export As a co-owner, what share of this land am I taken to own (s 22(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I hold it as a joint tenant`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other owners hold the land as joint tenants (not as tenants in common)
      `how many owners there are`                           IS A NUMBER  @desc How many co-owners there are, including you
      `my share as a tenant in common, as a percentage`     IS A NUMBER  @desc If you hold as a tenant in common, your share of the land as a percentage (e.g. 25); ignored for joint tenants
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What share of this land am I taken to own, as a percentage` IS
    100 TIMES (`the co-owner's share, as a fraction (s 22(1), (2))` `I hold it as a joint tenant` `how many owners there are` `my share as a tenant in common, as a percentage`)

@export What is the total taxable value of all my taxable land in Queensland (ss 19, 22)?
GIVEN `the taxable value of the land I live in`                IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable value of the whole parcel you live in, in dollars (0 if you own no home in Queensland)
      `my share of the land I live in, as a percentage`        IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of that parcel as a percentage (100 if you own it alone)
      `the percentage of my share that is exempt`              IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your share is exempt as your home, as a percentage: 100 if wholly exempt, 0 if not, or the part the Commissioner apportioned to the home
      `the taxable value of my shares of all my other land`    IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable value of your share of every other taxable parcel you own in Queensland, added up, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the total taxable value of my taxable land` IS
    `the total taxable value (s 19)`
        (LIST (`Holding` WITH
                   `taxable value of the parcel`        IS `the taxable value of the land I live in`
                   `the owner's share, as a fraction`   IS `my share of the land I live in, as a percentage` DIVIDED BY 100
                   `the exempt fraction of that share`  IS `the percentage of my share that is exempt` DIVIDED BY 100)
              (`Holding` WITH
                   `taxable value of the parcel`        IS `the taxable value of my shares of all my other land`
                   `the owner's share, as a fraction`   IS 1
                   `the exempt fraction of that share`  IS 0))

@export Am I an absentee for land tax (s 31)?
GIVEN `I am an Australian citizen`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen
      `I hold a permanent visa`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a permanent visa under the Migration Act 1958 (Cwlth) (a New Zealand special category visa is not one)
      `I ordinarily live in Australia`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Australia (including its external territories) is where you ordinarily live
      `I was outside Australia at midnight on 30 June`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were outside Australia at midnight on 30 June starting the financial year
      `I was outside Australia for more than half of the year to 30 June` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were outside Australia for more than half of the 12 months ending at midnight on 30 June
      `I am a government officer away on duty`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Commonwealth or State public officer who is outside Australia in the course of your duties
      `I am working abroad for my Australian employer`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are outside Australia on duty for an employer in Australia who employed you continuously for the year before you left
      `my absence has lasted more than 5 years`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your absence from Australia has lasted longer than 5 years
GIVETH AN `Absentee answer`
DECIDE `Am I an absentee` IS
    `the absentee status (s 31)`
        (`Residence facts` WITH
            `is an Australian citizen`                                                       IS `I am an Australian citizen`
            `holds a permanent visa`                                                         IS `I hold a permanent visa`
            `ordinarily resides in Australia`                                                IS `I ordinarily live in Australia`
            `is absent from Australia at the liability date`                                 IS `I was outside Australia at midnight on 30 June`
            `was absent from Australia for more than half of the 12 months to the liability date` IS `I was outside Australia for more than half of the year to 30 June`
            `is a Commonwealth or State public officer absent on duty`                       IS `I am a government officer away on duty`
            `is absent on duty for an employer in Australia who employed them continuously for 1 year before the absence` IS `I am working abroad for my Australian employer`
            `the absence has lasted longer than 5 years`                                     IS `my absence has lasted more than 5 years`)

DECLARE `Land tax answer` IS ONE OF
    `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `I owe no land tax: my total taxable value is under the threshold`
    `not covered: land owned as a trustee or through a company (s 32(1)(b), Schedule 2, s 33)`

@export How much land tax do I owe this financial year (ss 19, 32, Schedule 1, Schedule 3)?
GIVEN `the total taxable value of my taxable land`  IS A NUMBER  @desc The total taxable value of all the taxable land you own in Queensland at midnight on 30 June, in dollars, leaving out exempt land (see the total taxable value question)
      `I am an absentee`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an absentee (see the absentee question)
      `I own the land as a trustee or through a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the land as a trustee or through a company, rather than as an individual for yourself
GIVETH A `Land tax answer`
DECIDE `How much land tax do I owe` IS
    IF `I own the land as a trustee or through a company`
    THEN `not covered: land owned as a trustee or through a company (s 32(1)(b), Schedule 2, s 33)`
    ELSE IF `the tax` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `I owe land tax, in dollars, of` `the tax`
         ELSE `I owe no land tax: my total taxable value is under the threshold`
    WHERE
        `the tax` MEANS `the land tax of an individual (s 32(1)(a), (c))` `the total taxable value of my taxable land` `I am an absentee`

@export How much more land tax would I pay as an absentee than as a resident, on the same land (s 32(1)(c), Schedule 3)?
GIVEN `the total taxable value of my taxable land`  IS A NUMBER @desc The total taxable value of all the taxable land you own in Queensland, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much more land tax would I pay as an absentee` IS
    (`the land tax of an individual (s 32(1)(a), (c))` `the total taxable value of my taxable land` TRUE)
        MINUS (`the land tax of an individual (s 32(1)(a), (c))` `the total taxable value of my taxable land` FALSE)

§§ `Is my home exempt? (ss 22(3), 35 to 42)`

@export Is my land used as my home for this financial year (ss 36, 37, 38)?
GIVEN `I lived only here for the 6 months to 30 June`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lived on this land, and on no other land, continuously for the 6 months ending at midnight on 30 June (alone or with others)
      `this is my principal place of residence on 30 June`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this land is your principal place of residence at midnight on 30 June, even if you have lived here for less than 6 months
      `I was in care during those 6 months`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during all or part of those 6 months, you were a hospital inpatient, in residential aged care, or living on land you do not own in someone else's care
      `I lived only here before going into care`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before you went into care, you lived on this land and no other land
      `I have lived only here for at least 6 months in a row` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at some time you lived on this land, and no other land, for at least 6 consecutive months
      `months since I last lived here for 6 months`           IS A NUMBER  @desc If you are in care: the number of months from the end of the last period of at least 6 consecutive months you lived here to midnight on 30 June (0 if not in care)
      `the land earned income in the year to 30 June`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone earned income from use of the land in the 12 months ending at midnight on 30 June
      `all that income was rent from letting it be occupied`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all that income came from a lease, licence or other arrangement giving someone the right to occupy the land
      `it was let for no more than 6 months of that year`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the right to occupy lasted no more than 6 months of those 12 months
      `the rent only covered council rates and upkeep`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the income was no more than reasonably needed to cover the council rates and charges on the land and its maintenance
      `I am living elsewhere while my home is rebuilt or renovated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at midnight on 30 June, you are temporarily living elsewhere because the home is being demolished and rebuilt, or renovated so that it has to be vacated
      `this was my principal place of residence at some time in those 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this land was your principal place of residence at some time in the 6 months ending at midnight on 30 June
      `I intend to move back before next 30 June`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to live here again as your principal place of residence before midnight on the next 30 June
GIVETH A `Use as a home`
DECIDE `Is my land used as my home` IS
    `the use of the land as a home (ss 36 to 38)` (`my home use facts` `I lived only here for the 6 months to 30 June` `this is my principal place of residence on 30 June` `I was in care during those 6 months` `I lived only here before going into care` `I have lived only here for at least 6 months in a row` `months since I last lived here for 6 months` `the land earned income in the year to 30 June` `all that income was rent from letting it be occupied` `it was let for no more than 6 months of that year` `the rent only covered council rates and upkeep` `I am living elsewhere while my home is rebuilt or renovated` `this was my principal place of residence at some time in those 6 months` `I intend to move back before next 30 June`)

GIVEN `a` IS A BOOLEAN, `b` IS A BOOLEAN, `c` IS A BOOLEAN, `d` IS A BOOLEAN, `e` IS A BOOLEAN, `f` IS A NUMBER, `g` IS A BOOLEAN, `h` IS A BOOLEAN, `i` IS A BOOLEAN, `j` IS A BOOLEAN, `k` IS A BOOLEAN, `l` IS A BOOLEAN, `m` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Home use facts`
`my home use facts` `a` `b` `c` `d` `e` `f` `g` `h` `i` `j` `k` `l` `m` MEANS
    `Home use facts` WITH
        `used this land, and no other land, for residential purposes continuously for the 6 months ending at the liability date` IS `a`
        `uses this land as their principal place of residence at the liability date`             IS `b`
        `received care during all or part of those 6 months`                                     IS `c`
        `used this land, and no other land, as their residence before starting to receive care`  IS `d`
        `has used this land, and no other land, as their residence for at least 6 consecutive months` IS `e`
        `months from the end of the last such 6 months to the liability date`                    IS `f`
        `income was derived from use of the land in the year ending at the liability date`       IS `g`
        `all of that income was from a lease, licence or other right to occupy the land`         IS `h`
        `the right to occupy was for no more than 6 months of that year`                         IS `i`
        `the income was no more than reasonably needed for council rates and charges and maintenance` IS `j`
        `is temporarily living elsewhere at the liability date because of demolition and rebuilding, or renovation requiring the home to be vacated` IS `k`
        `used this land as their principal place of residence at some time in those 6 months`     IS `l`
        `intends to resume using it as their principal place of residence before the next 30 June` IS `m`

GIVEN `lettings` IS A NUMBER, `allowable` IS A BOOLEAN, `half` IS A BOOLEAN, `family` IS A BOOLEAN, `works` IS A BOOLEAN, `ordinary` IS A BOOLEAN, `other` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Other use facts`
`my other use facts` `lettings` `allowable` `half` `family` `works` `ordinary` `other` MEANS
    `Other use facts` WITH
        `number of lettings`                                                                   IS `lettings`
        `each letting is of a residential area the occupant lives in, not sublet, at no more than market rent, and not 1 of 3 or more flats in a building the principal resident does not live in` IS `allowable`
        `the let areas together are no more than 50% of the floor area of all residential areas` IS `half`
        `at least 1 letting is to a member of the principal resident's family`                  IS `family`
        `a person who lives there works there as an employee under an arrangement with their employer` IS `works`
        `that work is of a kind for which residential land is ordinarily used`                  IS `ordinary`
        `the land is used for any other purpose`                                                IS `other`

@export Which of the factors the Commissioner may weigh point to this land being my principal place of residence (s 36(2))?
GIVEN `months I have lived here`                    IS A NUMBER  @desc How many months you have occupied a residence on this land
      `my family lives here`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family lives here
      `I have moved my belongings in`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have moved your personal belongings into the residence
      `my electoral roll address is here`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your address on the electoral roll is this land
      `the services are connected`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether services such as telephone, electricity and gas are connected to the land
      `I bought it to live in as my main home`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acquired the land intending to live there as your principal place of residence
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Which factors point to this being my principal place of residence` IS
    `the s 36(2) factors that point to the land`
        (`Principal place of residence factors` WITH
            `months the person has occupied a residence on the land`      IS `months I have lived here`
            `the person's family lives there`                              IS `my family lives here`
            `the person has moved their personal belongings in`            IS `I have moved my belongings in`
            `the person's electoral roll address is the land`              IS `my electoral roll address is here`
            `telephone, electricity, gas or similar services are connected` IS `the services are connected`
            `the person acquired the land intending to occupy it as their principal place of residence` IS `I bought it to live in as my main home`)

@export If I rent out a room, work from home or use my home for something else, can the Commissioner treat it as used for a non-exempt purpose (ss 39, 40)?
GIVEN `how many lettings there are`                IS A NUMBER  @desc How many people (or households) you have given a right to live in part of your home under a lease, licence, or boarding or lodging arrangement (0 if none)
      `each letting is an allowable letting`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether each one lives in the part let, has not sublet any of it, pays no more than market rent, and the part is not one of 3 or more flats in a building you do not live in
      `the let parts are at most half the floor area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the let parts together are no more than 50% of the floor area of all residential areas on the land (every building, part of a building or other place of accommodation on the land that is used or available for use for living in; a shed or garage counts only if it is)
      `at least one letting is to my family`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one is let to a member of your family (spouse, parent, grandparent, brother, sister, nephew, niece, child, stepchild or grandchild, or certain of their spouses, or your spouse's parents, grandparents, siblings, nephews or nieces)
      `someone here works from home for their employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone who lives here works here as an employee under an arrangement with their employer
      `that work is ordinary home work`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that work is of a kind residential land is ordinarily used for, such as office work in a study (not, for example, manufacturing in a shed)
      `the land is used for anything else`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is used for any other purpose besides your home, the lettings and the work from home (for example a shop, a hairdressing room, a repair shed, or short-term letting)
GIVETH A `Non-exempt purpose answer`
DECIDE `Can my home be treated as used for a non-exempt purpose` IS
    `the non-exempt purpose question (ss 39, 40)` (`my other use facts` `how many lettings there are` `each letting is an allowable letting` `the let parts are at most half the floor area` `at least one letting is to my family` `someone here works from home for their employer` `that work is ordinary home work` `the land is used for anything else`)

@export Which of the factors the Commissioner must weigh point to the other use of my home being substantial (s 39(3))?
GIVEN `someone else has a right to occupy part of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone other than you has been given a right to occupy part of the land under a lease, licence, or boarding or lodging arrangement
      `employees or contractors work on the land`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone other than you or a family member who lives here works on the land as an employee or contractor, other than on the land itself or its buildings
      `part of the land is set aside for the other use`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether part of the land is used, or set aside, for the other purpose (for example two rooms kept for a hairdressing business)
      `last year's gross income from the land`              IS A NUMBER  @desc The gross income from business or any income-producing activity on the land in the previous financial year, in dollars
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Which factors point to the other use being substantial` IS
    `the s 39(3) factors that point to substantial use`
        (`Substantial use factors` WITH
            `someone other than the principal resident has a right to occupy part of the land under a tenancy agreement` IS `someone else has a right to occupy part of the land`
            `someone other than the principal resident or a resident family member works on the land as an employee or contractor, not on the land or its buildings` IS `employees or contractors work on the land`
            `part of the land is used or set aside for the other purpose`                          IS `part of the land is set aside for the other use`
            `gross income from business or an income producing activity on the land last financial year` IS `last year's gross income from the land`)

@export Is my home exempt from land tax this financial year (ss 22(3), 41, 42)?
GIVEN `I own it as a trustee, through a company or as a time-share manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own this land as a trustee, through a company, or as the manager of a time-sharing scheme
      `my home is on more than one parcel`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your home is spread over more than one separately valued parcel of land
      `I own it with others`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own this land with one or more co-owners (including a spouse)
      `I lived only here for the 6 months to 30 June`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lived on this land, and on no other land, continuously for the 6 months ending at midnight on 30 June (alone or with others)
      `this is my principal place of residence on 30 June`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this land is your principal place of residence at midnight on 30 June, even if you have lived here for less than 6 months
      `I was in care during those 6 months`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during all or part of those 6 months, you were a hospital inpatient, in residential aged care, or living on land you do not own in someone else's care
      `I lived only here before going into care`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before you went into care, you lived on this land and no other land
      `I have lived only here for at least 6 months in a row` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at some time you lived on this land, and no other land, for at least 6 consecutive months
      `months since I last lived here for 6 months`           IS A NUMBER  @desc If you are in care: the number of months from the end of the last period of at least 6 consecutive months you lived here to midnight on 30 June (0 if not in care)
      `the land earned income in the year to 30 June`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone earned income from use of the land in the 12 months ending at midnight on 30 June
      `all that income was rent from letting it be occupied`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all that income came from a lease, licence or other arrangement giving someone the right to occupy the land
      `it was let for no more than 6 months of that year`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the right to occupy lasted no more than 6 months of those 12 months
      `the rent only covered council rates and upkeep`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the income was no more than reasonably needed to cover the council rates and charges on the land and its maintenance
      `I am living elsewhere while my home is rebuilt or renovated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at midnight on 30 June, you are temporarily living elsewhere because the home is being demolished and rebuilt, or renovated so that it has to be vacated
      `this was my principal place of residence at some time in those 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this land was your principal place of residence at some time in the 6 months ending at midnight on 30 June
      `I intend to move back before next 30 June`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to live here again as your principal place of residence before midnight on the next 30 June
      `how many lettings there are`                IS A NUMBER  @desc How many people (or households) you have given a right to live in part of your home under a lease, licence, or boarding or lodging arrangement (0 if none)
      `each letting is an allowable letting`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether each one lives in the part let, has not sublet any of it, pays no more than market rent, and the part is not one of 3 or more flats in a building you do not live in
      `the let parts are at most half the floor area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the let parts together are no more than 50% of the floor area of all residential areas on the land (every building, part of a building or other place of accommodation on the land that is used or available for use for living in)
      `at least one letting is to my family`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one is let to a member of your family (spouse, parent, grandparent, brother, sister, nephew, niece, child, stepchild or grandchild, or certain of their spouses, or your spouse's relatives of those kinds)
      `someone here works from home for their employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone who lives here works here as an employee under an arrangement with their employer
      `that work is ordinary home work`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that work is of a kind residential land is ordinarily used for, such as office work in a study
      `the land is used for anything else`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is used for any other purpose besides your home, the lettings and the work from home
GIVETH A `Home exemption answer`
DECIDE `Is my home exempt` IS
    `the home exemption (ss 22(3), 41, 42)`
        `I own it as a trustee, through a company or as a time-share manager`
        `my home is on more than one parcel`
        `I own it with others`
        (`my home use facts` `I lived only here for the 6 months to 30 June` `this is my principal place of residence on 30 June` `I was in care during those 6 months` `I lived only here before going into care` `I have lived only here for at least 6 months in a row` `months since I last lived here for 6 months` `the land earned income in the year to 30 June` `all that income was rent from letting it be occupied` `it was let for no more than 6 months of that year` `the rent only covered council rates and upkeep` `I am living elsewhere while my home is rebuilt or renovated` `this was my principal place of residence at some time in those 6 months` `I intend to move back before next 30 June`)
        (`my other use facts` `how many lettings there are` `each letting is an allowable letting` `the let parts are at most half the floor area` `at least one letting is to my family` `someone here works from home for their employer` `that work is ordinary home work` `the land is used for anything else`)

§§ `Moving house (ss 42A, 42B, 44A)`

-- SITUATION: owning two homes across a 30 June because of a move.

@export I have moved into my new home: is my old home exempt this financial year (s 42A)?
GIVEN `my new home is exempt for me this 30 June`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home you now live in is exempt or partly exempt for you as your home at this midnight on 30 June
      `I did not own my new home last 30 June`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not yet own the home you now live in at the previous midnight on 30 June
      `I have owned my old home since last 30 June`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have owned your old home continuously since the previous midnight on 30 June
      `my old home was exempt for me last 30 June`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your old home was exempt or partly exempt for you as your home at the previous midnight on 30 June
      `I will have sold my old home by next 30 June`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will no longer own your old home at the next midnight on 30 June
      `I got rent from my new home before moving in`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received rent or other profits from your new home before you lived in it
      `the tenant of my new home left in time`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought the new home with a tenant in it and the tenant gave you vacant possession by the end of the lease or within 6 months of your purchase, whichever was earlier
      `I got rent from my old home after moving out`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received rent or other profits from your old home after you stopped living in it
GIVETH AN `Old home answer`
DECIDE `Is my old home exempt while I move` IS
    `the old home exemption (s 42A)`
        (`Old home facts` WITH
            `the current home is exempt or partly exempt for the person under s 41 or 42 at this liability date` IS `my new home is exempt for me this 30 June`
            `the person did not own the current home at the previous liability date`         IS `I did not own my new home last 30 June`
            `the person has owned the old home continuously since the previous liability date` IS `I have owned my old home since last 30 June`
            `the old home was exempt or partly exempt for the person under s 41 or 42 at the previous liability date` IS `my old home was exempt for me last 30 June`
            `the person will no longer own the old home at the next liability date`          IS `I will have sold my old home by next 30 June`
            `the person received rents or profits from the current home before living in it` IS `I got rent from my new home before moving in`
            `the current home was bought subject to a lease and the tenant gave vacant possession by the end of the lease or within 6 months of the purchase, whichever was earlier` IS `the tenant of my new home left in time`
            `the person received rents or profits from the old home after they stopped living in it` IS `I got rent from my old home after moving out`)

@export I have bought a new home but not yet moved: is my new home exempt this financial year (s 42B)?
GIVEN `my present home is exempt for me this 30 June`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home you live in now is exempt or partly exempt for you as your home at this midnight on 30 June, other than only because you are away during a renovation or rebuild
      `I will have sold my present home by next 30 June`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will no longer own the home you live in now at the next midnight on 30 June
      `I did not own the new home last 30 June`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not yet own the new home at the previous midnight on 30 June
      `the new home can be lived in this 30 June`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new home is capable of being lived in at this midnight on 30 June
      `the new home will be exempt for me next 30 June`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new home will be exempt or partly exempt for you as your home at the next midnight on 30 June
      `I will still own the new home next 30 June`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will still own the new home at the next midnight on 30 June
      `I got rent from my present home after moving out`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received rent or other profits from your present home after you stopped living in it
      `I got rent from the new home before moving in`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received rent or other profits from the new home before you lived in it
      `the tenant of the new home left in time`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought the new home with a tenant in it and the tenant gave you vacant possession by the end of the lease or within 6 months of your purchase, whichever was earlier
GIVETH A `New home answer`
DECIDE `Is my new home exempt before I move` IS
    `the new home exemption (s 42B)`
        (`New home facts` WITH
            `the current home is exempt or partly exempt for the person under s 41 or 42 at this liability date, other than under s 38` IS `my present home is exempt for me this 30 June`
            `the person will no longer own the current home at the next liability date`       IS `I will have sold my present home by next 30 June`
            `the person did not own the new home at the previous liability date`              IS `I did not own the new home last 30 June`
            `the new home can be lived in at this liability date`                             IS `the new home can be lived in this 30 June`
            `the new home will be exempt or partly exempt for the person under s 41 or 42 at the next liability date` IS `the new home will be exempt for me next 30 June`
            `the person will still own the new home at the next liability date`               IS `I will still own the new home next 30 June`
            `the person received rents or profits from the current home after they stopped living in it` IS `I got rent from my present home after moving out`
            `the person received rents or profits from the new home before living in it`     IS `I got rent from the new home before moving in`
            `the new home was bought subject to a lease and the tenant gave vacant possession by the end of the lease or within 6 months of the purchase, whichever was earlier` IS `the tenant of the new home left in time`)

@export After a moving exemption, must I tell the Commissioner what happened, and by when (s 44A)?
GIVEN `what happened`        IS A `Relevant matter` @desc What happened after the moving exemption: one of "none: the move went as assessed"; "s 44A(1)(a): the person still owns the old home at the next liability date"; "s 44A(1)(b): rents or profits were received in the way s 42A(3) describes"; "s 44A(2)(a): the person still owns the former home at the next liability date"; "s 44A(2)(b): the new home is not exempt or partly exempt for the person at the next liability date"; "s 44A(2)(c): the person does not own the new home at the next liability date"; "s 44A(2)(d): rents or profits were received in the way s 42B(3) describes"
      `the day it happened`  IS A DATE @desc The day that happened (for a matter at the next 30 June, that 30 June)
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commissioner about my move` IS
    IF `s 44A applies` `what happened`
    THEN `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` (`the last day to give a s 44A notice` `the day it happened`)
    ELSE `no: this section does not require me to give notice`

§§ `Renovating or rebuilding (ss 38, 44)`

-- SITUATION: away from home on 30 June because of building work.

@export After a renovation or rebuild exemption, if I have not moved back by the next 30 June, by when must I tell the Commissioner (s 44)?
GIVEN `my land tax was assessed on the basis that I was renovating or rebuilding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land tax for the year was assessed on the basis that your land was your home while you lived elsewhere for its demolition and rebuilding or renovation (s 38)
      `I moved back before the next 30 June`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you resumed living there as your principal place of residence before midnight on the next 30 June
      `the year of the next 30 June`                        IS A NUMBER  @desc The calendar year of that next 30 June
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commissioner I have not moved back` IS
    IF `s 44 applies` `my land tax was assessed on the basis that I was renovating or rebuilding` `I moved back before the next 30 June`
    THEN `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` (`the last day to give a s 44 notice` `the year of the next 30 June`)
    ELSE `no: this section does not require me to give notice`

§§ `Farm land (s 53, Land Tax Regulation 2021 s 2)`

-- SITUATION: land used for a business of primary production.

@export Is my land exempt as land used for primary production (s 53, Regulation s 2)?
GIVEN `how much of the land is used solely for the farming business` IS A `Extent of primary production use` @desc One of "all of the land is used solely for the business of primary production"; "part of the land is used solely for the business of primary production"; "none of the land is used solely for the business of primary production"
      `what the land is used for`                                    IS A `Primary production activity` @desc The activity carried on for the business, one of the Regulation s 2 activities (animals, cultivating land, plants or mushrooms, plantation trees, other agriculture, dairy farming or pasturage, or a directly related supporting activity) or "none of these activities"
      `I own the land as a trustee or through a company`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own this land as a trustee (for example of a family trust) or through a company, rather than as an individual for yourself
      `I am an absentee`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an absentee (see the absentee question)
GIVETH A `Primary production answer`
DECIDE `Is my farm land exempt` IS
    `the primary production exemption (s 53, Regulation s 2)` `how much of the land is used solely for the farming business` `what the land is used for` `I own the land as a trustee or through a company` `I am an absentee`

§§ `A deceased person's land (s 23)`

-- SITUATION: I am the executor, administrator or will trustee of someone who owned land.

@export As the executor or administrator, who is taken to own the deceased person's land for land tax (s 23(3), (4))?
GIVEN `I own the land as executor or administrator on 30 June` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at midnight on 30 June you own the land as executor, administrator or trustee under the will
      `the administration of the estate is complete`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the administration of the estate is complete
      `I have asked for the beneficiaries to be assessed`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Commissioner a request, in the approved form, to assess the beneficiaries as if they owned the land
GIVETH A `Deceased estate owner`
DECIDE `Who is taken to own the deceased person's land` IS
    `who is taken to own a deceased estate's land (s 23(3), (4))` `I own the land as executor or administrator on 30 June` `the administration of the estate is complete` `I have asked for the beneficiaries to be assessed`

@export Up to which 30 June can a deceased person's exempt land stay exempt (s 23(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the date of death` IS A DATE @desc The date the person died
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Up to which 30 June can the deceased person's land stay exempt` IS
    `the next 30 June after the date of death (s 23(5), (6))` `the date of death`

@export Is the deceased person's land exempt at the first 30 June after the death (s 23(4), (5))?
GIVEN `I own the land as executor or administrator on that 30 June` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at midnight on the first 30 June after the death you own the land as executor, administrator or trustee under the will
      `the administration was complete by that 30 June`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the administration of the estate was complete by midnight on that 30 June
      `I have asked for the beneficiaries to be assessed instead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Commissioner a request, in the approved form, to assess the beneficiaries as if they owned the land
      `the land was exempt at the last 30 June before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land (for example the person's home) was exempt land at the last midnight on 30 June before the death
      `how the land has been used since the death`               IS A `Use since the death` @desc One of "not used since the death"; "used since the death only for the purpose it was used for at the last 30 June before the death"; "used since the death for another purpose"
GIVETH A `Deceased estate exemption answer`
DECIDE `Is the deceased person's land exempt at the first 30 June after the death` IS
    `the deceased estate exemption at the next 30 June after the death (s 23(5))` `the owner under s 23` `the land was exempt at the last 30 June before the death` `how the land has been used since the death`
    WHERE
        `the owner under s 23` MEANS `who is taken to own a deceased estate's land (s 23(3), (4))` `I own the land as executor or administrator on that 30 June` `the administration was complete by that 30 June` `I have asked for the beneficiaries to be assessed instead`

§§ `Working abroad (ss 31(3)(b), 34)`

-- SITUATION: I am outside Australia on duty for my Australian employer.

@export I was assessed as not an absentee while working abroad: must I tell the Commissioner my absence has passed 5 years, and by when (s 34)?
GIVEN `I was assessed as not an absentee because I work abroad for my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land tax was assessed on the basis that you were not an absentee because you were abroad on duty for your Australian employer
      `my absence is longer than 5 years`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your absence from Australia has become longer than 5 years
      `the day I had been away 5 years`          IS A DATE    @desc The day on which you had been absent from Australia for 5 years
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commissioner that my absence has passed 5 years` IS
    IF `s 34 applies` `I was assessed as not an absentee because I work abroad for my employer` `my absence is longer than 5 years`
    THEN `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` (`the last day to give a s 34 notice` `the day I had been away 5 years`)
    ELSE `no: this section does not require me to give notice`

§§ `Telling the Commissioner (ss 76, 77, 77A; TAA s 28)`

@export Must I apply for my land to be exempt this financial year (s 76)?
GIVEN `it was exempt last financial year`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land was exempt land for the previous financial year
      `the ownership has not changed since`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ownership of the land is unchanged since then
      `it is still exempt under the same provision`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is still exempt for the same reason (for example still your home)
      `the Commissioner has told me it is believed exempt`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has given you a notice saying the Commissioner believes the land, or part of it, is exempt as your home for this financial year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply for the exemption` IF
    `an application in the approved form is needed (s 76)` `it was exempt last financial year` `the ownership has not changed since` `it is still exempt under the same provision` `the Commissioner has told me it is believed exempt`

@export My land was exempt last financial year but is not exempt at this 30 June: must I tell the Commissioner, and by when (s 77)?
GIVEN `it was exempt for the last financial year`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land was exempt land for the financial year just ended
      `it is no longer exempt at this 30 June`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at this midnight on 30 June the land is no longer exempt (for example you moved out and let it)
      `the ownership has not changed`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ownership of the land is unchanged
      `the year of this 30 June`                              IS A NUMBER  @desc The calendar year of this 30 June (the start of the new financial year)
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commissioner my land is no longer exempt` IS
    IF `s 77 applies` `it was exempt for the last financial year` `it is no longer exempt at this 30 June` `the ownership has not changed`
    THEN `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` (`the last day to give a s 77 or s 77A notice` `the year of this 30 June`)
    ELSE `no: this section does not require me to give notice`

@export Part of my land was exempt and that part has changed at this 30 June: must I tell the Commissioner, and by when (s 77A)?
GIVEN `part of it was exempt for the last financial year`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether only part of the land was exempt for the financial year just ended (for example part home, part business; or part used for primary production)
      `the exempt part has changed at this 30 June`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the part that is exempt has changed at this midnight on 30 June
      `the land is now not exempt at all`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is now not exempt at all (then the previous question applies instead)
      `the ownership has not changed`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ownership of the land is unchanged
      `the year of this 30 June`                              IS A NUMBER  @desc The calendar year of this 30 June
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commissioner the exempt part has changed` IS
    IF `s 77A applies` `part of it was exempt for the last financial year` `the exempt part has changed at this 30 June` `the land is now not exempt at all` `the ownership has not changed`
    THEN `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` (`the last day to give a s 77 or s 77A notice` `the year of this 30 June`)
    ELSE `no: this section does not require me to give notice`

@export I have learned my land tax assessment is too low: must I tell the Commissioner, and by when (TAA s 28)?
GIVEN `my assessment is wrong and I owe more`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have become aware that your assessment was not, or is no longer, correct and that your correct land tax is more than the amount assessed
      `the day I became aware`                 IS A DATE    @desc The day you became aware of it
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commissioner my assessment is too low` IS
    IF `my assessment is wrong and I owe more`
    THEN `yes: I must give the Commissioner notice no later than` (`the last day to advise an under-assessment (TAA s 28(2))` `the day I became aware`)
    ELSE `no: this section does not require me to give notice`

§§ `Paying (TAA s 30; ss 70 to 74, Land Tax Regulation 2021 s 4)`

DECLARE `Payment date answer` IS ONE OF
    `I must pay in full by the date stated in the notice` HAS `the date` IS A DATE
    `the stated date is less than the 30 days TAA s 30(2) requires, unless the Commissioner has stated an earlier date under TAA s 33; the earliest s 30(2) date is` HAS `the date` IS A DATE

@export By what date must I pay my land tax in full (TAA s 30(1)(e), (2))?
GIVEN `the day the assessment notice was given to me` IS A DATE @desc The day your land tax assessment notice was given to you
      `the date for payment stated in the notice`     IS A DATE @desc The date stated in the notice as the date by which the tax must be paid
GIVETH A `Payment date answer`
DECIDE `By what date must I pay my land tax` IS
    IF `the stated date is at least 30 days after the notice is given (TAA s 30(2))` `the day the assessment notice was given to me` `the date for payment stated in the notice`
    THEN `I must pay in full by the date stated in the notice` `the date for payment stated in the notice`
    ELSE `the stated date is less than the 30 days TAA s 30(2) requires, unless the Commissioner has stated an earlier date under TAA s 33; the earliest s 30(2) date is` (`the earliest date for payment TAA s 30(2) allows` `the day the assessment notice was given to me`)

@export Can I pay this land tax by instalments (s 70)?
GIVEN `the kind of assessment` IS A `Kind of land tax assessment` @desc What your assessment notice is: one of "an assessment by the Commissioner that is not a default assessment or a reassessment" (the usual annual notice); "a default assessment"; "a self assessment"; "a reassessment of land tax"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I pay by instalments` IF
    `the land tax may be paid by instalments (s 70)` `the kind of assessment`

@export By what date must I elect to pay my land tax by instalments (s 72, Regulation s 4)?
GIVEN `the day the assessment notice was given to me`  IS A DATE    @desc The day your land tax assessment notice was given to you
      `the Commissioner has allowed me longer`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has allowed you a longer period to elect
      `the last day the Commissioner allowed`           IS A DATE    @desc If so, the last day of the longer period (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I elect to pay by instalments` IS
    `the last day to elect to pay by instalments (Regulation s 4(a))` `the day the assessment notice was given to me` `the Commissioner has allowed me longer` `the last day the Commissioner allowed`

@export How much is each of my 3 land tax instalments (ss 71(5), 73(2))?
GIVEN `my land tax` IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax assessed, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is each instalment` IS
    `each instalment (s 73(2))` `my land tax`

@export On what dates are my 3 land tax instalments due (s 71(4))?
GIVEN `the day the assessment notice was given to me` IS A DATE @desc The day your land tax assessment notice was given to you
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
DECIDE `On what dates are my instalments due` IS
    LIST (`the stated date of instalment` 1 `after a notice given on` `the day the assessment notice was given to me`)
         (`the stated date of instalment` 2 `after a notice given on` `the day the assessment notice was given to me`)
         (`the stated date of instalment` 3 `after a notice given on` `the day the assessment notice was given to me`)

DECLARE `Missed instalment answer` HAS
    `the outstanding land tax I must now pay in full, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `I must pay it no later than`                                 IS A DATE
    `unpaid tax interest runs from`                               IS A DATE

@export I missed a land tax instalment: how much must I now pay, by when, and from when does interest run (s 74)?
GIVEN `my land tax`                                    IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax assessed, in dollars
      `which instalment I missed`                      IS A NUMBER @desc Which instalment was not paid by its date: 1, 2 or 3 (the earlier ones having been paid)
      `the day the assessment notice was given to me`  IS A DATE   @desc The day your land tax assessment notice was given to you
      `the date for payment in full stated in the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date stated in the notice by which the tax must be paid in full if not paid by instalments
GIVETH A `Missed instalment answer`
DECIDE `I missed an instalment: what now` IS
    `Missed instalment answer` WITH
        `the outstanding land tax I must now pay in full, in dollars` IS `the outstanding land tax after missing instalment` `which instalment I missed` `of` `my land tax`
        `I must pay it no later than`                                 IS `the date by which the outstanding land tax must be paid (s 74(2))` `which instalment I missed` `the day the assessment notice was given to me` `the date for payment in full stated in the notice`
        `unpaid tax interest runs from`                               IS `the start date for unpaid tax interest after a missed instalment (s 74(3))` `the date for payment in full stated in the notice`

§§ `Interest and penalty tax (TAA ss 54, 58)`

@export From what date does unpaid tax interest run on my land tax (TAA s 54(5)(c))?
GIVEN `the due date`                                IS A DATE   @desc The date by which the land tax had to be paid (for a missed instalment, the date for payment in full stated in the notice)
      `the days I was late with a required notice`  IS A NUMBER @desc If you did not give a notice or information the law required for this assessment (such as a s 77 notice) on time, the number of days it was late, counting the day you gave it (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what date does unpaid tax interest run` IS
    `the start date for unpaid tax interest (TAA s 54(5)(c))` `the due date` `the days I was late with a required notice`

@export How much unpaid tax interest do I owe on late land tax (TAA s 54)?
GIVEN `the unpaid land tax`                          IS A NUMBER @desc The land tax (primary tax) unpaid, in dollars
      `the prescribed interest rate`                 IS A NUMBER @desc The prescribed annual interest rate under the Taxation Administration Regulation, as a percentage (e.g. 10.5)
      `the due date`                                 IS A DATE   @desc The date by which the land tax had to be paid
      `the days I was late with a required notice`   IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days a required notice or information for this assessment was late, counting the day it was given (0 if none)
      `the day I paid in full`                       IS A DATE   @desc The day you paid the land tax in full
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much unpaid tax interest do I owe` IS
    `the unpaid tax interest (TAA s 54)` `the unpaid land tax` `the prescribed interest rate`
        (`the days of interest, both dates inclusive (TAA s 54(2))` (`the start date for unpaid tax interest (TAA s 54(5)(c))` `the due date` `the days I was late with a required notice`) `the day I paid in full`)

@export What is the most penalty tax I can be charged on this assessment (TAA s 58)?
GIVEN `what kind of assessment it is`              IS AN `Assessment kind` @desc One of "an original assessment that is not a default assessment"; "a default assessment under TAA s 13(1)(a) or (b)" (made because you did not lodge or give something required, or it was unsatisfactory); "a reassessment of a default assessment under TAA s 13(1)(a) or (b)"; "a reassessment of another assessment"
      `the land tax on this assessment`            IS A NUMBER @desc The primary land tax on this assessment or reassessment, in dollars
      `the land tax on the original assessment`    IS A NUMBER @desc The primary land tax on the original assessment, in dollars
      `the lowest land tax on an earlier reassessment` IS A NUMBER @desc The lowest primary land tax on any earlier reassessment, in dollars (the original figure if there was none)
      `I failed to tell the Commissioner my assessment was too low, or hindered the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied you did not tell the Commissioner within 30 days that your assessment was too low (TAA s 28), or hindered the Commissioner from learning your liability
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most penalty tax I can be charged` IS
    `the most penalty tax (TAA s 58(3))`
        (`the penalty tax (TAA s 58(1), (2))` `what kind of assessment it is` `the land tax on this assessment` `the land tax on the original assessment` `the lowest land tax on an earlier reassessment`)
        `I failed to tell the Commissioner my assessment was too low, or hindered the Commissioner`

§§ `Unpaid land tax on land I bought (ss 59, 60)`

-- SITUATION: land bought from someone who may have left land tax unpaid.

@export Can the Commissioner recover unpaid land tax on this land from me as its owner now (s 59)?
GIVEN `the tax was imposed before I bought the land`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unpaid land tax (with its interest and penalty tax) was imposed before you purchased the land
      `I got a clearance certificate showing none unpaid`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you obtained a clearance certificate stating there was no unpaid land tax on the land at the time of your purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can unpaid land tax be recovered from me` IF
    `unpaid land tax can be recovered from the owner for the time being (s 59)` `the tax was imposed before I bought the land` `I got a clearance certificate showing none unpaid`

@export Is my land subject to the first charge for unpaid land tax (s 60)?
GIVEN `I bought it for value and in good faith`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought the land for value (you paid for it) and in good faith
      `I got a clearance certificate showing none unpaid`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you obtained a clearance certificate stating there was no unpaid land tax on the land at the time of your purchase
      `I got a clearance certificate showing security is held`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you obtained a clearance certificate stating that the Commissioner holds security (a bank guarantee or cash deposit) for the unpaid land tax
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my land subject to the charge for unpaid land tax` IF
    `the first charge has effect against the person (s 60)` `I bought it for value and in good faith` `I got a clearance certificate showing none unpaid` `I got a clearance certificate showing security is held`

§§ `Objecting and appealing (s 81; TAA ss 63 to 69)`

-- SITUATION: I disagree with my assessment.

@export Can I object to my land tax assessment on this ground (s 81; TAA ss 63, 64)?
GIVEN `what I want to object to`                   IS AN `Assessment objected to` @desc One of "an original assessment, not a compromise assessment" (the usual annual notice); "a compromise assessment"; "a reassessment increasing the liability"; "a reassessment under TAA s 18(b) decreasing the liability"; "another reassessment"
      `my ground is that the valuation is too high` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your ground is that the Land Valuation Act value of the land is excessive
GIVETH AN `Objection answer`
DECIDE `Can I object on this ground` IS
    `the right to object (TAA ss 63, 64; s 81)` `what I want to object to` `my ground is that the valuation is too high`

@export By what date must I lodge my objection (TAA s 65)?
GIVEN `the day the assessment notice was given to me` IS A DATE    @desc The day the assessment notice you object to was given to you
      `the Commissioner has extended my time`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has extended the time for you to object (possible where it would be unreasonable to require it within 60 days)
      `the extended last day`                          IS A DATE    @desc If so, the last day of the extended time (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I lodge my objection` IS
    `the last day to lodge an objection (TAA s 65(1)(d), (2))` `the day the assessment notice was given to me` `the Commissioner has extended my time` `the extended last day`

@export Can I appeal to the Supreme Court or apply to QCAT about the decision on my objection, and by when (TAA s 69)?
GIVEN `my objection was allowed completely`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner allowed your objection completely
      `the day the decision notice was given to me`         IS A DATE    @desc The day the Commissioner's written notice of the decision on your objection was given to you
      `I have paid all the tax and late payment interest`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the whole of the land tax and late payment interest payable under the assessment
      `today`                                               IS A DATE    @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH AN `Appeal or review answer`
